    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "That's an interesting summary. To be more specific, though, how do these theories apply when looking at the actual differences we see in society today? For instance, when researchers look at disparities in standardized testing or socioeconomic achievement between different racial groups, what do the biological or evolutionary perspectives say about whether those gaps are linked to these different cognitive or temperamental traits?",
